<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Golden Gate (Kyiv)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1037</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Golden Gate of Kyiv, Golden Gate of Kiev</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Golden Gate was the main ceremonial entrance of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>, built under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-the-wise">Yaroslav the Wise</a> around 1037 as part of the city's new fortifications, with a church above its passage. It was badly damaged when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> sacked Kyiv in 1240 and later fell into ruin. The surviving remains were enclosed in a reconstruction in 1982. The gate served as a model for the Golden Gate of Vladimir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/golden-gate-kyiv.jpg" alt="Golden Gate (Kyiv)" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Chernilevsky · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Golden_Gate_Kiev_2018_G1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
